      "id": "cymbeline/sceneII_7.2/p@56109",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "IMOGEN.\nI have read three hours then. Mine eyes are weak;\nFold down the leaf where I have left. To bed.\nTake not away the taper, leave it burning;\nAnd if thou canst awake by four o’ th’ clock,\nI prithee call me. Sleep hath seiz’d me wholly.",
